speechtext:
I would welcome an
opportunity for discussing the matter of patronage in Nova Scotia and, indeed, elsewhere in Canada, a little nearer home to my hon. friend than Nova Scotia. If I had followed the example of his political friends in Nova Scotia, there might be some reason for complaint. Bu-t I endeavoured to deal with these matters on the broad basis of the -best interests of the country. If my hon. friend has any particular instance in mind, he is quite at liberty to bring it up. I am not going to weary the committee this afternoon, but during the last two or three years there have occurred in connection with political patronage on the part of the provincial administration, friends of my hon. friends, certain matters which might well afford an excuse for my friends to feel, as indeed they do feel and have so expressed themselves very often, that I do not deal with these matters as aggressively as they would like.	;

Fisheries Act Amendment
